   "sql": "SELECT *\nFROM courses AS c\nJOIN instructors AS i ON i.id = c.instructor_id\nWHERE c.code = 'CS301'",
   "note": "ON names the pair of columns: the course's instructor_id against the instructor's id. one teacher, and every column of both tables, so dept appears twice.",
